      body: 'Here is a made-up story to hold the idea. A girl named Leilani in Hawaii kept a shoebox of photographs from the year her family lost their house in a storm. There was the roof in the yard, the wet sofa, the motel room where five of them slept. Whenever she felt low she took the box down and looked through it, and she felt lower. One afternoon her auntie came by with a second shoebox. It was from the same year. Here were the neighbors on the roof with hammers. Here was the church kitchen full of rice and chicken. Here was her little brother laughing in the motel pool. Leilani had forgotten every one of them. Her auntie did not take the first box away, and she did not say the storm had not been bad. She only set the second box beside it and said they belonged on the same shelf. After that Leilani took them down together. The storm was still in the pictures. So were the mercies. "It is of the LORD’s mercies that we are not consumed, because his compassions fail not." (Lamentations 3:22)',
